## 10. RECENT CHANGES (November 2026 Session)

Changes made during the current development session, some committed and some pending local commit:

1. **Email CC**: Added `emailCcAddress` field to PlatformSettings. Rewrote `lib/email.ts` to auto-fetch and merge global CC address (5-min cache). Added CC address input to Admin > Settings UI.

2. **Admin payment notification**: When a booking results in PENDING_PAYMENT status (bank transfer/offline), all active admins receive an email notification using the `payment-pending-admin.tsx` template.

3. **Admin/Coordinator Book Slot**: New feature allowing admin and coordinators to book classes on behalf of parents. Files: `admin/book-slot/page.tsx`, `admin/book-slot/BookSlotClient.tsx` (shared), `coordinator/book-slot/page.tsx`, `api/admin/book-slot/route.ts`. Parent's Browse Teachers nav item is being disabled.

4. **Timezone fix — `convertAvailabilitySlots`**: Extended reference dates from 7 to 21 days to fix cross-day-boundary slot conversion between IST and US timezones (the "Sunday slots missing" bug).

5. **Timezone fix — RescheduleModal**: Added `teacherTimezone` to the `teacher-slots` API response and passed it to the `RescheduleModal` component. Changed default fallback from "America/New_York" to "Asia/Kolkata".

6. **Pricing fix (pending)**: The BookSlotClient pricing resolution needs a grade dropdown (similar to the parent's TeacherProfileClient) so that TeacherSubjectRate lookup uses the correct gradeBandId instead of falling to the teacher's default rate.

---

## 11. PENDING ISSUES / KNOWN BUGS

1. **Pricing in BookSlotClient**: The admin booking page may show the teacher's base rate ($18) instead of the configured subject-specific rate ($22) when the student's grade doesn't resolve to a grade band. Fix requires adding a grade selector and passing `allGrades` prop.

2. **Parent Browse Teachers**: This flow is being deprecated but the code still exists. If re-enabled, it needs the same timezone fixes applied to the reschedule modal.

3. **CCAvenue DNS**: Some US customers can't resolve `www4.ipg-online.com`. This is a client-side DNS issue, not application code. Advise customers to use Google DNS (8.8.8.8) or Cloudflare DNS (1.1.1.1). Do NOT change the gateway URL without consulting Fiserv — credentials are cluster-specific.

4. **Build warnings**: Multiple `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` and `react/no-unescaped-entities` ESLint warnings exist across the codebase. These are non-blocking (warnings, not errors) but should be cleaned up over time.

---

## 12. HOW TO WORK WITH THIS CODEBASE

When asked to modify code, always: (1) Read the actual file from the repo first — do not guess field names or types. (2) Cross-reference against `prisma/schema.prisma` for database field names. (3) Check whether the component uses named or default exports. (4) Add explicit type annotations to all `.map()`/`.filter()` callbacks in server components. (5) Use `Number()` when serializing Prisma Decimal fields. (6) Test with `npm run build` (not just IDE type checking) since `next build` performs a stricter full-project type check. (7) When adding timezone-dependent features, always pass the teacher's actual timezone from the server — never rely on defaults.

